<title>BRAZIL: Brazil southern soybean region to remain dry-Somar.</title>
<headline>Brazil southern soybean region to remain dry-Somar.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's southern soybean regions should see dry weather throughout the coming week, with an approaching cold front only expected to bring rain to coastal regions, independent meteorologists Somar said.</p>
<p>A high pressure area, which is preventing cold fronts from entering the country, should only begin to weaken in the middle of next week, it added.</p>
<p>Rainfall in the past week and the historical monthly average in key states in millimeters was as follows:  </p>
<p> STATE	    TOTAL RAIN   TOTAL RAIN    AVERAGE    AVERAGE</p>
<p>			     May 1-5     April	 April	May</p>
<p> Londrina (PR)		 0	   52	   100	  90</p>
<p> Cascaval (PR)		 0	   25	    95	  85</p>
<p> Passo Fundo (RS)	    0	   70	   128	 140</p>
<p> Sao Luiz Gonzaga (RS)    1.1	 138	   177	 150</p>
<p> Santa Maria (RS)	   0.6	  68	   141	 141</p>
<p> Mato Grosso		  3.0	  93	   115	  52</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
